---
import { AFFILIATE_NOTE, ESMA_REGISTER_URL } from '../config.ts';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base title="Affiliate links" description="How SolLock labels affiliate links to exchanges, and what they mean for you.">
  <h1 class="section-title">Affiliate links</h1>
  <div class="prose">
    <p>
      Under "Need Solana first?" on the lock page are exchanges where you can buy Solana. The note right under the links says what
      they are: "{AFFILIATE_NOTE}" The exchange pays that commission, and your price stays the same.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>Exchanges are listed alphabetically.</li>
      <li>A sign-up offer shown with an exchange is that exchange's own, with its conditions, and can differ by country.</li>
      <li>Choose an exchange yourself, and check first that it is authorised by the financial regulator where you live. In the EU, that is the <a href={ESMA_REGISTER_URL}>ESMA register</a>.</li>
      <li>Crypto prices can fall, and you can lose money.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</Base>
